# B.6
sub1("The battery leads with connected discourse because the pre-registered task-count probe of section 5.15 found that for mild cognitive impairment picture description is the weakest of five tasks and performs at chance, while two discourse tasks together beat three picture tasks together (+0.079 [+0.004, +0.158]); picture description is retained unchanged for the dementia target, where it alone has an externally evaluated model behind it. Story recall uses an examiner-supplied story retold immediately, so no cultural knowledge of a narrative is required, in the paradigm of Craft Story 21 of the NACC Uniform Data Set; procedural discourse requires no stimulus material, which makes it the one task that survives intact in a paper fallback, and making tea is chosen because every participant has performed it hundreds of times. Elicitation is fixed and logged because word count is the strongest single mild-impairment marker on connected discourse (section 5.10.1), so variable elicitation would record examiner behaviour, and because the flagged healthy speakers of the locked external corpus had described the picture genuinely thinly while a minimum-length rule was tested and refused (section 5.13): for every task and every participant the prompt is read verbatim, the maximum duration is enforced, the re-prompt rule is at most two probes using the exact wording *\"tell me anything else you can\"*, each after 10 s of silence, and elicitation time and probe count are recorded as metadata. The Qur'anic probe additionally records which surah was recited, self-reported familiarity, approximate age at memorisation and any formal tajweed training, the confounders without which recitation accuracy is uninterpretable.",
     "The battery leads with connected discourse because the pre-registered task-count probe of section 5.15 found that for mild cognitive impairment picture description is the weakest of five tasks and performs at chance, while two discourse tasks together beat three picture tasks together (+0.079 [+0.004, +0.158]); picture description is retained unchanged for the dementia target, where it alone has an externally evaluated model behind it. Story recall uses an examiner-supplied story retold immediately, so no cultural knowledge of a narrative is required, in the paradigm of Craft Story 21 of the NACC Uniform Data Set; procedural discourse requires no stimulus material, so it is the one task that survives intact in a paper fallback, and making tea is chosen because every participant has performed it hundreds of times. Elicitation is fixed and logged because word count is the strongest single mild-impairment marker on connected discourse (section 5.10.1), so variable elicitation would record examiner behaviour, and because the flagged healthy speakers of the locked external corpus had described the picture thinly while a minimum-length rule was tested and refused (section 5.13): for every task and every participant the prompt is read verbatim, the maximum duration is enforced, the re-prompt rule is at most two probes using the exact wording *\"tell me anything else you can\"*, each after 10 s of silence, and elicitation time and probe count are recorded. The Qur'anic probe additionally records which surah was recited, self-reported familiarity, approximate age at memorisation and any formal tajweed training, the confounders without which recitation accuracy is uninterpretable.")
